# Requirements Confidence And Small Diffs

- On non-trivial tasks, get enough clarity on scope, constraints, and success criteria before coding.
- If an unknown could affect correctness, compatibility, security, or safety, stop and ask instead of guessing.
- Define pass/fail acceptance criteria before implementation.
- Prefer small, independently testable diffs that are easy to review and roll back.
- Touch only the files needed for the current diff; avoid opportunistic refactors or format churn.
- Follow the standing dependency policy. Prefer stdlib and existing dependencies; do not add third-party packages without approval.
- When a task needs planning first, stop after the plan and wait for approval before implementing the first diff.
